-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Defensive Stance loses its damage penalty
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Defensive Stance: Damage done reduction removed."
--
-- Where the stance actually lives.  Spell 71 is only the shapeshift
-- (SPELL_AURA_MOD_SHAPESHIFT, MiscValue 18 = FORM_DEFENSIVESTANCE); it carries
-- none of the numbers.  The three stat effects are on the passive 7376, which
-- is why 71's description reads them back out as $7376s1 / $7376s2 / $7376s3:
--
--   Effect1  SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_TAKEN  -11 -> -10%   (kept)
--   Effect2  SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_DONE    -6 ->  -5%   (removed here)
--   Effect3  SPELL_AURA_MOD_THREAT                  44 -> +45%   (kept)
--
-- Effect2 is blanked rather than zeroed: an aura effect left in place with an
-- amount of 0 still applies, still shows in the aura list, and still costs a
-- modifier lookup on every damage calculation.  Effect = 0 means core never
-- builds the AuraEffect at all.
--
-- Why.  Alonecraft is a solo fork -- the tank is also the damage dealer, and
-- there is no raid to hand the DPS role to.  A 5% damage tax on the only stance
-- in which a Protection warrior can use Shield Slam, Revenge, Shield Block and
-- (after woa_2026_08_09_01.sql) Mocking Blow is a tax on playing the spec at
-- all.  It also compounds badly with normalised rage: rage income is now a
-- fixed ceiling (Rage.Normalized = 1), so damage lost can no longer be bought
-- back with more swings.
--
-- Both descriptions are rewritten.  Leaving $7376s2 in 71's prose would render
-- "and damage caused by 0%" once the effect is gone, and leaving $s2 in 7376's
-- would do the same in the spellbook.
--
-- Spells:
--   71   = Defensive Stance (the shapeshift, description only)
--   7376 = Defensive Stance Passive (the three stat effects)
-- ============================================================

